.Dd February 17, 2026
.Dt TESSERACT-SUPERVISOR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tesseract-supervisor
.Nd monitor and restart tesseract-daemon on crashes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar tesseract-daemon args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a process supervisor for
.Xr tesseract-daemon 1 .
It forks and executes
.Nm tesseract-daemon ,
monitors it, and automatically restarts it if it crashes.
All arguments are passed through to the daemon.
.Pp
The daemon path is derived from the location of
.Nm
itself.
If
.Nm
is invoked as
.Pa /usr/local/bin/tesseract-supervisor ,
it will execute
.Pa /usr/local/bin/tesseract-daemon .
If invoked without a path, it looks for
.Nm tesseract-daemon
via
.Ev PATH .
.Sh BEHAVIOR
On a clean exit (exit code 0) from the daemon,
.Nm
exits 0.
.Pp
On a crash (signal death or non-zero exit code),
.Nm
logs the event to standard error, waits 1 second, and restarts the daemon.
.Pp
If the daemon crashes 5 times within 60 seconds,
.Nm
gives up and exits with an error.
.Pp
On receipt of
.Dv SIGINT
or
.Dv SIGTERM ,
.Nm
forwards the signal to the daemon.
If the daemon does not exit within 3 seconds, it is killed with
.Dv SIGKILL .
.Nm
then exits 0.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start the supervisor with default settings:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
tesseract-supervisor -d ./tessdata
.Ed
.Pp
Start on a custom port:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
tesseract-supervisor -p 8000 -d /usr/local/share/tessdata
.Ed
.Pp
Stop cleanly:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kill $(pgrep tesseract-supervisor)
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Nm
logs all events to standard error with a
.Qq supervisor:
prefix.
.Pp
Exit status is 0 on clean shutdown, or 1 on error
(including rapid crash protection).
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr tesseract-daemon 1 ,
.Xr tesseract 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Renaud Allard
